pySMESH: the viscous layer builder of Cartesian_3D frees the offset makers it creates (SMESH
V9_16_0; applies after StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL_duplicate_nodes.patch).

Defect: each compute of Cartesian_3D with viscous layers, and each shrink of the two-step
ViscousLayerBuilder, leaks one BRepOffset_MakeOffset per solid.

Symptom: 20 computes of a 2 x 2 x 2 box at spacing 0.1 with layers on every face, each in a
fresh mesh that is then closed. With the offset TmpMesh freed
(StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D_offset_mesh_leak.patch), the private bytes still grow by 1.06 MB per
compute; the same loop with no layers grows by 0.10 MB.

Root cause: ViscousBuilder::MakeOffsetSolid makes each maker with new
(StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx:913) and keeps it in _makeOffsetCollection (:930), which
getOffsetSubShape reads for the offset history. ~ViscousBuilder (:882-885) deletes only
_offsetMesh. A maker that fails is in no collection, and the return at :957 drops it.

Change, in StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx only: ~ViscousBuilder deletes every maker in
_makeOffsetCollection, and the failure branch deletes its maker before it returns.

Not changed: the offset shapes, their history, and every mesh.
diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx
--- a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx
+++ b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.cxx
@@ -886,6 +886,9 @@
 StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL::ViscousBuilder::~ViscousBuilder()
 {
   delete _offsetMesh; //_offsetMesh = 0;
+  // pySMESH: MakeOffsetSolid makes these with new; nothing else frees them
+  for ( BRepOffset_MakeOffset* makeOffset : _makeOffsetCollection )
+    delete makeOffset;
 }
 
 //================================================================================
@@ -957,6 +960,7 @@
         theError = "operation not done.";
       }
       theError = "BRepOffset_MakeOffset error: " + theError;
+      delete makeOffset; // pySMESH: not in _makeOffsetCollection, so freed here
 
       return TopoDS_Shape();
     }    
